From: mscharged-port
Subject: Port: Online waits for Recharged's update
Upstream-base: 8b9d92dd88b4c727cc6359ee4cd5ba128cced7b8

Enforced updates (owner 2026-11-12). Players who skipped an update met
newer versions online, and their games went out of sync. The launcher now
installs a newer release by itself. When that fails, or the game starts
without it, the game's own check (the host's src/launcher/online_gate.h)
keeps Online closed: an official release plays online only while it is the
newest release and could check that. Test builds and local builds are never
held back.

SHMainMenu::SelectItem asks mscharged_tweak_online_locked before its own
Online checks; when it says so, the main menu shows the Online save data
popup (POPUP_ONLINE_SAVE_DATA_REQUIRED, one OK) with the port's message
instead of entering Online, and stays on the menu like after that popup.
FEPopupMenu::Create takes the message from
mscharged_tweak_take_online_lock_message for that popup only, and only once
the lock asked for it; every other popup keeps its text.

diff --git a/include/mscharged_tweaks.h b/include/mscharged_tweaks.h
--- a/include/mscharged_tweaks.h
+++ b/include/mscharged_tweaks.h
@@ -233,6 +233,12 @@
 // captain that trains.
 int mscharged_tweak_training_item_count(void);
 bool mscharged_tweak_training_item_giant(void);
+// Enforced updates (tweak patch 0054, the host's src/launcher/online_gate.h):
+// whether the main menu keeps Online closed, because this release is not the
+// newest one or could not check (a check still running gets up to 3 s); then,
+// once, the message of the popup that says so.
+bool mscharged_tweak_online_locked(void);
+const unsigned short* mscharged_tweak_take_online_lock_message(void);
 
 #ifdef __cplusplus
 }
